Share one owner across all columns in duckdb_data_chunk_from_arrow

duckdb_data_chunk_from_arrow moved the input ArrowArray into the first column's
scan state and gave every other column a wrapper with a null release callback.
Zero-copy columns keep their scan state's wrapper alive as vector auxiliary
data, so the whole array's buffers were owned by column 0's vector alone: once
that vector was released (e.g. a projection or a caller referencing a subset of
the columns), the remaining columns pointed at freed Arrow buffers. Take
ownership once and share the wrapper with every column.

